  "notes": "Male/female duet country-pop built on unison-and-thirds trio harmony and piano-led ballads. The harmonic core is documented as an instrument choice, not a chord choice: \"piano and synthesizer are the harmonic core,\" with two electric guitars — one rhythm, one for a single melodic solo — so the counter is a sustained pad answering rather than a lick trade, and the chord voicing sits open and low under the vocal. Drums are \"restrained and dry; cross-stick or hats verse, snare from the chorus, no big fills; the ballads keep the kit under the piano throughout,\" which is a near-zero fill count and the quietest accent tier in this batch. The bass is \"sustained roots under verses, 8ths under choruses; low and unobtrusive.\" Harmony is \"I–V–vi–IV and vi–IV–I–V\" with the signature ballad's identity being \"an extended piano intro over a slow four-chord loop\" — hence the long intro in the arrangement block and the real `2_bars_per_chord` weight. The duet architecture is the melodic parameter the entry actually names: one voice takes verse 1, the other verse 2, both in unison or thirds for the chorus, \"the emotional peak is a shared held note.\" ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: high-medium); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the counter ratio and the arrangement section lengths.",
